From b73f2cce612630bd25dadc5c54ffaa1ebc454ded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:18:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Sun shadows with shapes: heroes, creatures, buildings and
 small things cast

The first films of the sun shadows (#263) found a broad darkening and not
one object-shaped shadow. Four faults in 0065 kept the casters a player
looks at out of the map, or out of the filter:

- Every skinned body drew far outside the map. The pass writes a caster's
  rig slot into its instance row as a float's value (37.0), and the
  caster shader read it back with bitcast<u32>, slot 1 108 606 976 for
  slot 37. Heroes, creatures, rigged game objects and animated doodads
  (trees with their own sway) all went. It now reads u32().
- Skinned gear and riders carry NoFrustumCulling, so Bevy gives them no
  Aabb, and the extract skipped every mesh without one. A skinned part is
  now bounded on its rig's origin, where its palette draws it, by its
  bind-pose box plus a margin, or a loose 3 yd sphere with no box.
- A building's interior WMO groups never cast, and they hold its walls
  and roof as often as its rooms. They cast now; props inside still don't.
- On high, the PCSS blocker search sampled a ring of six taps whose
  nearest is 0.17 yd out, and read a narrower shadow (a post's, a
  rail's) as lit. It now samples the receiver's own texel first.

The broad darkening is not the filter shading the ground itself (a test
of flat ground under the lowest sun reads 0.96 lit or better on every
slice): with the casters above missing, what darkened was the terrain's
own relief and the canopies, without the shapes standing in them.

lookshadow map <slice> | off draws a slice of the shadow map in the top
right corner, the world as the sun sees it, so the next films show what
the casters left in it.

Revised after the second films (#269, take 271):

- The pumpkins cast nothing, at Brackwell's 10:00, 15:00 and 17:30, on low
  as on high, and the field's strongbox neither: the patch's doodads and the
  server's gather nodes alike. A batch 1.12 draws alpha-blended (M2 blend
  mode 2) cast nothing at all, and many solid props draw that way, their
  texture's alpha whole where the object is; it never reached the static
  pass either, which takes only opaque and alpha-tested batches. A blended
  batch that writes and tests depth now casts, cut by its texture at 1.12's
  alpha-test reference (224/255), so glass, smoke or a soft card, well under
  it, still casts nothing; additive, multiply and depth-less ones never.
  WOW_SHADOW_STATS now counts the blended meshes casting, and the model
  meshes left out and why (hidden, unbounded, outside, not casting).
- A hero's shadow in full sun at 10:00 read faint and very soft. On the
  film it is there, figure-shaped, but its darkest part takes about a third
  of the ground's light, and its edges blur wide. The penumbra was the
  filter's radius, not its width, so 0.035 blurred like a sun four degrees
  wide: it is 0.012 now (about 1.4 degrees; a head 2.4 yd up blurs 0.06 yd,
  a canopy 12 yd up 0.3 yd). A full shadow takes 0.95 of the sun, was
  0.85; the ambient stays whole.
- The test that checks a caster shades the point under it now stands a
  2 yd hero and a pumpkin on flat ground, the map drawn from them as the
  pass draws it, and reads the ground under the torso, the head, a leg and
  the pumpkin through the receivers' filter on low and high.

Revised after the third films (#269, take 273):

- The pumpkins still cast nothing, and every shadow line said "0 blended
  meshes cast": the second round's rule never fired. It cast a blended
  batch only if it wrote depth, and 1.12 draws many solid props blended
  with M2 render flag 0x10 (no depth write) set. A blended batch now casts
  cut by its texture whether it writes depth or not; one that skips the
  depth test, an additive or a multiply one still never, nor an opaque or
  alpha-tested batch that writes no depth (a glow shell), nor its fade twin.
- WOW_SHADOW_STATS=1 now lists, once a second, every model mesh within
  25 yd of the camera ("[shadows near]"), nearest first: its distance, its
  verdict (casts solid, cut or blended, or left out: hidden, unbounded,
  outside every slice, or not casting and why: no depth test, additive,
  multiply, indoors on the interior-prop lane, ...), what spawned it (doodad,
  building, creature, game object) and its 1.12 blend, the material's alpha
  mode, marker word and flags, and its texture's path, which names the
  model's folder. No WoW data is on the machine this was written on, so
  what the pumpkin and the strongbox are is for the next film's log to say.
  (The strongbox stands in the Brackwell barn: on the interior-prop lane
  it casts no sun shadow by design, and the list says so.)
- The hero's shadow (take 273: crisp, the ground under it at 0.62 of its
  light) is unchanged.

